 "reading": "Not an edge, and the #913 observation does not carry over to Europe. The US cash session does lead the European open through the gap (correlation of the prior US session with the DE40 / UK100 / EU50 gap +0.35 to +0.56), but the European session that follows neither reverses nor extends it: the correlation of the gap with the session after it is −0.04 to +0.00, and of the US session with the European session −0.05 to +0.02. Fading the triggered gaps is about zero before costs (−0.019R to +0.017R a trade in the six cells; UK100 + EU50 +0.002R in 2016 → now) and every cell loses after the 0.04 % round trip (about 0.03R at a one-ATR stop; month-sum t −0.57 to −4.09). The US-led subset (T3), the one the #913 mechanism describes, is the worst in 2016 → now (−0.034R gross, −0.063R net, below all 40 random-side placebos) and does not replicate the small positive gross figure of 2005-15 (+0.017R). The reversal seen on JP225 / HK33 was most likely a feature of those two markets or of noise, not a general response to a US-led gap. Never call this an edge and never propose it as a council system; nothing live changed. Post hoc, not a test: no other exit, stop or trigger was tried."
}
